1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,571
Your crush walks in, and your stomach flips.

2
00:00:02,571 --> 00:00:04,222
Here's what's really going on.

3
00:00:04,717 --> 00:00:09,406
Your brain flags this moment as a very big deal, and flips on fight-or-flight.

4
00:00:09,406 --> 00:00:11,089
Adrenaline floods your body.

5
00:00:11,583 --> 00:00:12,885
Your heart speeds up.

6
00:00:12,885 --> 00:00:16,171
Blood rushes to your muscles, and away from your gut.

7
00:00:16,171 --> 00:00:17,844
Digestion slows right down.

8
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:19,520
Here's the twist.

9
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:24,546
Your gut has its own nervous system, with 200 to 600 million nerve cells.

10
00:00:24,546 --> 00:00:27,368
Some scientists call it the second brain.

11
00:00:27,883 --> 00:00:30,056
Like and subscribe for more Crush Files.

12
00:00:30,356 --> 00:00:34,918
And the vagus nerve, your gut-brain hotline, mostly carries messages up.

13
00:00:34,918 --> 00:00:38,402
Eight or nine of every ten fibers report to your brain.

14
00:00:38,917 --> 00:00:41,578
So when blood leaves your gut, its nerves notice.

15
00:00:41,578 --> 00:00:44,023
Scientists think that's the flutter you feel.

16
00:00:44,517 --> 00:00:45,766
No real butterflies.

17
00:00:45,766 --> 00:00:47,514
Just your whole body saying:

18
00:00:47,514 --> 00:00:48,326
this matters.

19
00:00:48,326 --> 00:00:50,325
More Crush Files on the channel.
